---
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/app.css';
import '../styles/page.css';
---

<AppLayout
	title="About — doodleai.art"
	description="What doodleai.art is: chat with an agent, attach a photo, and get back a hand-drawn doodle avatar or collage. No accounts, bring your own API key."
>
	<Navbar />

	<main class="page">
		<div class="page-hero">
			<div class="eyebrow">About</div>
			<h1>A doodle booth you <span class="grad">chat</span> with</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				doodleai.art turns a photo into a hand-drawn doodle avatar or collage. Instead of a form,
				you talk to an agent: attach a photo (or just describe a character), say what you want, and
				it draws it.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="prose">
			<h2>The idea</h2>
			<p>
				Most "AI photo" tools are a picker full of filters. This one is a conversation — attach a
				photo, tell the agent what you're after, and it picks the right doodle style, generates it,
				and lets you keep refining ("thicker outline", "warmer paper") until it's right.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>No accounts.</strong> You bring your own PicX API key (free to get, see Settings),
				and everything you create — chats, saved doodles, saved reference photos — lives only in
				your browser.
			</p>

			<h2>How it works</h2>
			<ol class="steps">
				<li><b>Add a PicX API key.</b> One free key from PicX Studio, pasted into Settings. Nothing is stored on our servers.</li>
				<li><b>Start a chat.</b> Attach a photo, mention a saved character with @, or just describe someone for a surprise.</li>
				<li><b>The agent draws it.</b> It picks a skill — a single avatar, a close-up collage, a full-body action collage — and generates it.</li>
				<li><b>Keep it or refine it.</b> Ask for changes, remix, save to your moodboard, or download.</li>
			</ol>

			<h2>Bring your own key</h2>
			<p>
				Generation runs through PicX's API using <strong>your</strong> key, and the chat runs on a
				model via OpenRouter. That means no signup on our end, no subscription to us, and no
				middleman marking up the cost of generation — you deal with PicX and OpenRouter directly for
				anything beyond their free tiers.
			</p>

			<div class="facts">
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Login required</div>
					<div class="v">None</div>
				</div>
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Cost to use this site</div>
					<div class="v">Free</div>
				</div>
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Your data on our servers</div>
					<div class="v">None</div>
				</div>
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Skill needed</div>
					<div class="v">Zero</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h2>What this isn't</h2>
			<p>
				There's no feed, no public gallery, and nothing you make here is visible to anyone but you —
				your chats, moodboard, and saved characters stay in your browser's local storage. We don't
				build a profile of you and we don't see your API key, your photos, or your conversations
				beyond the single request needed to generate a reply.
			</p>

			<h2>Who made this</h2>
			<p>
				doodleai.art is a small side project — built fast, deployed on Cloudflare's edge. It's
				the kind of thing that exists because it was fun enough to ship.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="page-cta">
			<a href="/">Start doodling →</a>
		</div>
	</main>

	<Footer />

	<script>
		import { initThemeToggle } from '../lib/theme';
		const themeToggle = document.getElementById('themeToggle');
		if (themeToggle) initThemeToggle(themeToggle);
	</script>
</AppLayout>
